    "title": "Trading cooler temperatures for the heat in Columbus, Ga - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylee Barbee ,\n6 hours ago\nCOLUMBUS, Ga. (WRBL)- Happy Wednesday! We hope you enjoyed the cooler weather over the past few days, because we have a warm up on the way.\nThursday: Temperatures tomorrow are set to warm into the 90s across the region. Lows will still sit in the lower-60s. Plus, we are still in for plenty of sun.\nWeekend: Temperatures are expected to remain stable in the lower 90s this weekend. Saturday, the winds will pick back up briefly in the afternoon.\nNext Week: The dry forecast will continue next week. Expect plenty of sun and no rain. Temperatures are expected to continue climbing into the mid-90s by Monday, making readings above average. Morning lows will warm into the upper 60s.\nJust a reminder: We are 12 days away from the official start of Fall on September 22nd!\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WRBL.\n1",
